docs/receipts/hv/hv-r3-log-parts-1.params.json:13:      "content": "HV-R3-RESULT-PART 002\ne: hv-r3-provenance-summary.json, hv-r3-native-provenance.json and CLI help/version receipts.\n\nAM7 PASS. A-01 through A-12 name the superseded foundation clauses. A-05 now explicitly retires foundation 6.7 model-grade sequences/nested activities and agent_context_grader_not_allowed; the amended internal grade origin/state guard uses retryable conflict. Manual hostile status/receipt ingestion, single grader and HvMaxTurns assumptions are retired, while response trust and the separate HostileReview context remain. The base foundation raw-byte SHA-256 is 6E5D4F418E78CF9A76AB366F64D4F24002C09E3C3F024502ED89D77C6E77295E, matching the claim. Evidence: hv-r3-foundation-hash.json, foundation 6.5/6.7 and amendment 179-190,1243-1281.\n\nAM8 PASS. Independent catalog comparison: 63 proposed FR/TR/TEST records, 21 FR roots, 21 mappings with 42 edges, 138 FR acceptance criteria, 146 named-test occurrences and 145 distinct names. All 1269 field/status/criterion/test/mapping checks pass. Every criterion is bound exactly once: H1 13, H2 19, H3 35, H5 17, H6 19, H7 34, shared 1. H1 adapter/Pester harness cases are distinct from server-launched and live cases. The seven existing records and eleven mapping edges in 19.3 have unchanged substantive content; read-generated timestamps are not edits. RequirementsWorkflow.cs generates UtcNow on read at 963-964,1021-1022,1085-1086,1133. Evidence: hv-r3-catalog-comparison.json, hv-r3-phase-continuity.json, hv-r3-d09-semantic-diff.json. This PASS concerns the exact catalog and bindings, not completeness of the behavior criticized in AM3/AM9.\n\nAM9 FAIL. P1 through P15 match base source/store/receipts and REMED-HVPIPELINE-001, including the unsatisfied HOSTILEREVIEW-003 criterion 4, SESSIONLIFE-005 criteria 2 and 1, and hook miscitations. P5 is correctly split between H0 text retirement and H3 configured/default artifact worker. P10-P15 match the six Codex PR81 comments posted after merge; federation D5 forbids the suggested automatic migration, and approved foundation SESSIONTURN-005 AC001/AC004 forbids the suggested Stop auto-close. That foundation record is not yet in this workspace store. Section 20.4 assigns named tests to the approved owning designs. However, the new artifact worker cannot yet fulfill all unchanged execution-metadata criteria. Evidence: hv-r3-source-problems-1.txt through -4.txt, live store captures, GitHub PR/comment/activity captures and R3-F04.\nRequired edits: R3-F04. Each is specified below; no operator decision is needed.\n\nAM10 PASS. The live PLAN-HVPIPELINE-001 and REMED-HVPIPELINE-001 were read in full through workflow.todo.get. The plan derives from section 20, preserves NOT APPROVED/code freeze, D-03, operator-named Codex gpt-6-astra max for this plan work, prior-round records, H6 before H5 and the four-phase requirements/interfaces-stubs/green mocked TDD/implementation discipline. H0 precedes HvStorageSchema and HvSharedComponents; production order is H1,H2,H3,H7,H4,H6,H5, followed by separate-instance integration/live checks. No clause authorizes production code before approval. This PASS does not approve the deficient architecture the plan references.\n\nAM11 PASS. Amendment standing rules, H0/H1 and G1-G6 use Nuke for every build/test, Octopus only for release orchestration, PowerShell for designed scripts/tools and a separate temporary integration/live instance. GitHub Actions and Azure Pipelines are not gates/evidence. The approved foundation Node material is not silently authorized for this new design; amendment surfaces require PowerShell. No product build, test or live-server integration was run by this document-only review.\n\nAM12 PASS. SPDX Apache-2.0 header, zero prohibited dash characters and zero table rows in the amendment. All 18 effort commits carry the marker-required agent/model/effort/confidence signature. Known-marker-key and credential-pattern scan of 268 unique changed blobs, commit messages and both TODOs found no secret. Live GitHub activity has 18 entries: one branch creation and 17 ordinary pushes, zero force_push; the old audit matches its ten-entry prefix through caaa41b0 and all eight later pushes are ordinary pushes through 9e682224. src/plugins/core/tests have no changes from base. Evidence: hv-r3-hygiene.json and captured git/activity commands.\n\nAM13 FAIL. The required closure list is 13 PASS and 5 FAIL. R2-F03/F08/F09/F10 and round 1 F18 retain the precise defects below. The other required closures pass, and the seventeen round 1 items round 2 passed remain credited. The artifact sweep repair has an unfixed HV sibling, while the audited read and corruption fixes introduced incomplete boundaries/propagation. Claims in remediation commit 67297000 and its follow-ups that these areas are complete are therefore not accepted.\nRequired edits: R3-F01, R3-F02, R3-F03, R3-F04, R3-F05, R3-F06. Each is specified below; no operator decision is needed.\n\nEvery FAIL, its evidence and its required correction:\n\nR3-F01 FAIL: A second lease sweep can requeue a newer or completed HV request. Classification: implementer edit.\nLocation: docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md:1124; docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md:1136; docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md:1453; docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md:1747; FR-MCP-HVPIPE-007-AC003.\nDefect: ExpireHvRunLeasesCommand selects active expired runs before its per-run transaction, but inside that transaction rechecks only expiry. It does not recheck active status or whether this is still the request current attempt, and abandonment does not release or clear the expired lease. HvRetryDecision then changes the request without a terminal-state guard.\nEvidence: Contract counterexample, not an execution of proposed code: sweep A and sweep B both select expired run R. A abandons R and queues its request. A new run R2 is claimed and may complete. B enters its transaction for R: the old expiry still has passed, so B abandons R again and applies HvRetryDecision to the now Running or Completed request. It becomes Queued or Failed, possibly releasing turns and emitting a false terminal notification. The artifact-worker sweep at 1747 explicitly rechecks active state and refuses an accepted request; that round 2 repair was not propagated to the HV sweep. SerializableWrite cannot repair a stale candidate unless its delegate revalidates the state.\nChange to PASS: Make expiry an idempotent, guarded transition in the transaction: re-read active run status, current ownership/attempt and request eligibility, and skip an already settled or superseded candidate. Ensure terminal requests cannot be revived. Cover two sweepers with an intervening claim and an intervening successful finalization, with named tests in FR/TR/TEST-MCP-HVPIPE-007 at H3 and the finalization case at H7; update the policy, unit, caller diagrams and phase bindings.\n\nR3-F02 FAIL: A probe consumes evidence before its read audit is durable. Classification: implementer edit.\nLocation: docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md:161; docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md:371; docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md:380; docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md:1055; docs/architecture/SessionTurn-Review-AgentContext-Architecture-Amendment-1-Durable-HV.md:1414; FR-MCP-HVPIPE-018-AC003.\nDefect: RecordRead enlists its ledger row in the caller transaction when one exists. CloseHvRunOutputCommand then consumes and verifies the probe chunks inside that same transaction. The read audit is only committed