docs/receipts/hv/hv-r3-verdict-parts.json:5:    "Body": "<!-- SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0 -->\n2026-10-18T01:58:29 - Independent hostile validation, amendment1-r3, one round.\n\nOverallVerdict DISAGREE. Accuracy 95/100, completeness 92/100, confidence 98/100. AM1 to AM13: 7 PASS, 6 FAIL, 0 UNKNOWN. Six material implementer edits; zero operator-decision failures. Required prior-item closure: 13 PASS, 5 FAIL. Scores judge the functionality of the proposed architecture and plan, not an arithmetic fraction of checks. The audit, recovery and execution contracts prevent 98/98 despite exact catalog synchronization and substantial repaired coverage.\n\nScope: class 1 project architecture and derived plan at HEAD 9e6822246e0e13f51612c638bc72d148954ccc18 on docs/hv-architecture-amendment-20261016, based on 36783b79. BDPv4 constrains the plan structure, not this read-only operation. No implementation is claimed or authorized. No source edits, commits, pushes, other agents, public comments, TODO/requirement/triage/memory/settings writes, or other session changes were made. Only this reviewer own session and receipts were written. Review time was unbounded; progress was emitted during the run. The source foundation/federation plans were examined only where cited.\nTimestampUtc: 2026-10-18T06:58:29.7290117+00:00\nTimestampLocal: 2026-10-18T01:58:29 (US/Central, local display only). Time-bearing HV data remains UTC per D-08.\nValidatorIdentity: Codex CLI, gpt-6-astra, effort max. Live own rollout /home/sharpninja/.codex/sessions/2026/10/18/rollout-2026-10-18T01-18-11-01a14da9-1b10-75e2-bfac-c13091d343b1.jsonl; thread/session_meta 01a14da9-1b10-75e2-bfac-c13091d343b1; turn_context 10/18/2026 06:18:12 explicitly records model=gpt-6-astra and effort=max. Subsequent turn_context records were independently checked with the same values in hv-r3-runtime-contexts.json. This is distinct from author Cline and implementer ClaudeCode/claude-opus-5-5/xhigh.\nReviewer sessionId: Codex-20261018T062121Z-plugin-session; requestId: req-20261018T062156Z-amendment1-r3.\nMandatory first actions, before validation: executed /home/sharpninja/.claude/skills/add-profile/SKILL.md and read every inventoried non-skill Markdown file in /home/sharpninja/.claude/profile/ in full. File count 1: PROFILE-MERGED.md. Repeated full reads after compaction. Read the entire root checkout AGENTS-README-FIRST.yaml in memory; recovered the display-truncated instruction range separately. Confirmation: full marker read, no marker scalar/key value copied to a receipt or log. Own session/turn opened using only the installed Codex mcpserver 1.120.0 wrapper, cache /tmp/hv-r3-codex-plugin-cache-20261018T011809 outside the worktree. Initial openSession invocation lacked a usable session id and was rejected; corrected from this plugin cache before beginTurn, which persisted. No Claude plugin wrapper or raw REST was used.\n\nPrimary receipts:\n- /home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.claude/worktrees/hv-amendment-20261016/docs/receipts/hv/hostile-validator-amendment1-r3-20261018T011809.md\n- /home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.claude/worktrees/hv-amendment-20261016/docs/receipts/hv/hostile-validator-amendment1-r3-20261018T011809.json\n- /home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.claude/worktrees/hv-amendment-20261016/docs/receipts/hv/20261018T011809-amendment1-r3.request.jsonl\n- /home/sharpninja/github/McpServer/.claude/worktrees/hv-amendment-20261016/docs/receipts/hv/20261018T011809-amendment1-r3.response.jsonl\n\nMandatory attack surfaces, scored separately:\n- 1. Requested claims and implementer assertions: FAIL; accuracy 95, completeness 92. All thirteen AM claims assessed; six material findings contradict completeness claims in the remediation and self-review. Counts, sources, current store and provenance independently checked.\n- 2. Workspace rules and artifact hygiene: PASS; accuracy 99, completeness 99. Reviewed artifacts preserve process/tool/approval rules; secrets, signatures, normal pushes and source freeze checked. Earlier implementer conduct is outside scope. Reviewer deviations are disclosed separately, never attributed to the implementation.\n- 3. Requirements, criteria, use cases and mappings: FAIL; accuracy 96, completeness 93. Catalog equality and phase assignment pass; audit/recovery and artifact metadata outcomes do not satisfy their existing requirements. Needed tests belong to existing FR/TR/TEST, not new operator decisions.\n- 4. Plan considered as a whole: FAIL; accuracy 96, completeness 94. Approval, phases, mock gate, integration isolation and done criteria are sound. The architecture is authoritative for H3/H7; its contradictory recovery/audit/data-flow rules cannot jointly satisfy those phases. The plan remains NOT APPROVED.\n\nClaim-by-claim assessment:\n\nAM1 FAIL. All 37 cited Cline quotation fragments match actual user-role source text; P-01 to P-07 and D-01/D-02/D-04/D-05/D-06/D-07/D-08/D-09 agree with the profile, handoff and operator answers. D-03 correctly remains operator-owned. D-07 assignment and D-09 unchanged records pass. The universal audit obligation S-29/R-19 is nevertheless contradicted by the read paths in R3-F02/F03. Sources: hv-r3-provenance-summary.json; hv-r3-d09-semantic-diff.json; amendment 42-84,152-173,2928-2936.\nRequired edits: R3-F02, R3-F03. Each is specified below; no operator decision is needed.\n\nAM2 FAIL. The document has 104 diagram blocks, all with matching final render sources; UC-HV-01 through UC-HV-12 and B.9 exist. Explicit units, nested activities and namespaces substantially improve the contract. The listed field/data-flow, component-user, caller-outcome and wire-shape contradictions remain. Evidence: hv-r3-diagram-source-check.json and each finding location.\nRequired edits: R3-F01, R3-F02, R3-F03, R3-F04, R3-F05, R3-F06. Each is specified below; no operator decision is needed.\n\nAM3 FAIL. W-01 through W-12 and I-01 through I-13 were traced. Atomic finalization, immutable accepted input, at-least-once outbox/watch inbox, cancellation at close, containment without a review deadline and bounded corrupt-payload retries are stated. HvProbeOutcome now owns all probe exits with the configuration guard and settled-probe restart rule. Double expiry, rollback of read audit and incomplete internal outcomes prevent the durability claim from passing.\nRequired edits: R3-F01, R3-F02, R3-F04, R3-F05. Each is specified below; no operator decision is needed.\n\nAM4 PASS. RunReviewerProcess/StreamReviewerOutput flush a single line after FlushInterval even with no next line. FR-MCP-HVPIPE-008-AC001 tests a single line then silence; AC003 uses a gated fake reviewer whose next step waits for observed live output. H1 adapter tests are separated from server/surface and live checks. Amendment 1502-1572,2694-2706,2813-2833. This is design adequacy, not a claim of implemented streaming.\n\nAM5 FAIL. HV entities participate in the ledger, mutation audit failure is a hard stop, removal is explicit, findings/hashes survive removal, and the ledger is append-only with no purge. Public retrieval and finalizer/brief reads have an explicit audit boundary. Probe consumption can lose its read audit and submission replay omits it. Amendment 156,161,285,369-383,1055,2772-2783.\nRequired edits: R3-F02, R3-F03. Each is specified below; no operator decision is needed.\n\nAM6 PASS. VI-01 through VI-08 and section 16.3 were checked against the 78-file original probe manifest and actual native CLI receipts, then current version/help outputs only. Versions: Codex 0.162.1, Claude 2.1.300, Cline 3.0.71, Grok 1.0.60, Copilot 1.0.98. Native Codex/Claude model and effort, Copilot requested-versus-actual behavior, Cline absence of successful-run effort provenance and Grok output match the bounded conclusions. Barrier and plugin-log qualification, configured Copilot max and storage-cost work remain explicit H1 gates, not claimed completed probes. The .NET multi-member GZIP receipt is a decode/negative-control proof, not storage-cost measurement. No other reviewer/probe was launched. Evidenc",
