7: /// <summary>
8: /// TR-MCP-USECASE-018 (AC-006), TR-MCP-USECASE-019 (AC-008): finds platform dependence in unit tests by reading
9: /// the C# syntax tree. A test that depends on the platform is an integration test (operator 2026-10-19: "If it
10: /// depends on the environment, it's an integration test."), so an operating-system check, an OS-platform
11: /// attribute, an xUnit skip, or a binding to the real process host is a finding unless the test method, its
12: /// test class, or an enclosing class carries <c>[Trait("Category", "Integration")]</c>. The compiler's parser
13: /// separates code from strings, comments and documentation and keeps the code inside interpolation holes, so a
14: /// member access split across lines, a qualified, global-qualified or aliased name, a <c>using static</c>
15: /// import, a method group, and an attribute anywhere in an attribute list are read like a plain call or
16: /// attribute; a name inside <c>nameof</c> is not a use. Every conditional-compilation branch is read: the file
17: /// is parsed once for each combination of the symbols its <c>#if</c> and <c>#elif</c> directives name, and a
18: /// file that names more than <see cref="MaxConditionalSymbols"/> symbols fails the scan instead of leaving a
19: /// branch unread. Test classes are types whose name ends in <c>Tests</c> or that declare a method with an
20: /// attribute whose name ends in <c>Fact</c> or <c>Theory</c>; other helper types (for example the host-neutral
21: /// <c>UnitTestPaths</c> fixture) are not test classes. An OS-platform attribute on the assembly or module is a
22: /// finding for the whole project. Limits: the scan reads one file's syntax, so dependence reached through a
23: /// helper type defined in another file, a global using or alias declared in another file, reflection, or
24: /// operating-system behavior of a base-library call such as <c>Path.GetFullPath</c> is outside it. Repository
25: /// reads are covered by construction instead: <see cref="FindRepositoryLocators"/> keeps the shared
26: /// <c>TestRepositoryRoot</c> the only repository-root locator (DRY), and that locator refuses to resolve outside
27: /// an integration test, so a unit test that reads the checkout through any helper fails the unit run.
28: /// </summary>
29: internal static class UnitSuitePlatformScanner
