53:     /// <summary>
54:     /// TR-MCP-USECASE-018 (AC-006): the one definition of an xUnit skip shared by this scanner and the skip guard.
55:     /// Returns the 1-based lines, in any conditional-compilation branch and in any type or none, that hold a skip
56:     /// call (<c>Assert.Skip</c>, <c>Assert.SkipWhen</c>, <c>Assert.SkipUnless</c>, <c>Skip.If</c>,
57:     /// <c>Skip.IfNot</c>), a use of <c>SkipException</c>, a <c>SkippableFact</c> or <c>SkippableTheory</c>
58:     /// attribute, or an attribute argument that sets a property whose name starts with <c>Skip</c> (for example
59:     /// <c>Skip</c>, <c>SkipUnless</c>, <c>SkipWhen</c> or <c>SkipExceptions</c> on a test or data attribute); an
60:     /// attribute is reported on the line of its name.
